,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kadazan people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kadazan_people,"The Kadazan people, together with the Dusun, the Rungus, the Bajau are believed to have origins linked to the Austronesian migration known as the ""Out of Taiwan"" theory. [67][68] According to this theory, the ancestors of the Kadazan were among the early Austronesian-speaking peoples who migrated from Taiwan thousands of years ago.",Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
1,Coastal Kadazan language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coastal_Kadazan_language,"Coastal Kadazan, also known as Dusun Tangara, is a dialect of Central Dusun as well as a minority language primarily spoken in Sabah, Malaysia. It is the primary dialect spoken by the Kadazan people on the west coast of Sabah especially in the districts of Penampang, Papar and Membakut (sub-district of Beaufort).",Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
2,Kadazan/Dusun Songs - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLW9p0H-qBD2HsZv8o2p_qgdXqJlSWT34h,"Listen to Kadazan/Dusun Songs on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.",Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
3,KadazanDusun Best Songs - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLbH9nhuAK4V3_XDGypCS5jPsD4fu2lVw1,Joan Jerome Sinding Kalangadan 80an (Artis Dusun Kadazan Sabah) Otai Channel • 2.4K views • 4 years ago,Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
4,"KadazanDusun People: Kaamatan, Sumazau & Sabah Culture",https://sabahguide.com/ethnic-groups/kadazan-dusun/,The Kadazan-Dusun's ancestors were among the original Austronesian farmers who brought wet rice cultivation to Borneo. Nunuk Ragang today is a recognised cultural heritage site.,Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
5,Sabahan/Kadazan Dusun Songs - playlist by nrdhlkrl | Spotify,https://open.spotify.com/playlist/2bGLkY1qBTt8jVuICwgGy4,Playlist · Sabahan/Kadazan Dusun Songs · 46 items · 6 saves,Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
6,Alat Muzik Tradisional Kaum Kadazandusun,https://www.scribd.com/doc/55065844/Alat-Muzik-Tradisional-Kaum-Kadazandusun,"tradisional ianya juga digunakan oleh suku kaum Bajau dan beberapa suku Dusun/Kadazan. Selalunya, ia dimainkan dalam majlis-majlis dan perayaan seperti majlis perkahwinan dan upacara keagamaan, di mana ianya diiringi oleh gong-gong tradisional. Alat ini merangkumi lapan ataupun 9 buah gong-gong cerek yang kecil.",Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
7,PDF alat_muzik_kadazandusun - Archive.org,https://archive.org/download/AlatMuzikDusunTambunan/alat_muzik_kadazandusun.pdf,"Keluarga-keluarga bahasa ini pula diklasifikasikan sebagai sebahagian daripada Stok Borneo yang merupakan sebahagian daripada Superstok Western Ausronesian yang termasuk di dalam bahasa-bahasa Austronesian. Keluarga bahasa Dusun mempunyai empat belas bahasa pertuturan, dengan bahasa Kadazandusun adalah bahasa yang terbesar (King dan King 1984).",Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
8,The Tongkungon: A traditional KadazanDusun plucked musical instrument ...,https://bioresources.cnr.ncsu.edu/resources/the-tongkungon-a-traditional-kadazandusun-plucked-musical-instrument-from-sabah-malaysia/,"Tongkungon music usually imitates the music of the gong ensemble. In the absence of a gong ensemble, these musical instruments are also played to accompany non-ritual dances performed in small groups (Matusky and Beng 2012). Although this musical instrument is a solo instrument, it can sometimes be played in a duet (Matusky and Beng 2012).",Kadazan Dusun,Austronesian
